{"sourceSha256": "488dc340e6b79ade391a29927f1906fbad425d3e69bcbd96fcbc739d86f4a4d3", "text": "© ¥i ta “Tl\n\n| Grade: B (360)\n\nThis is a pass but since you need 400, you have to be careful with the little\ndetails. You do not have to change all the words given in the case notes\n(e.g. you can maintain ‘grip strength’) as long as you can construct good\nsentences with them. Sometimes using the words in the case notes will\nmake more sense and can help you write faster as well (and leave you\n\nwith some time for proofreading).\n\nDr. John Smith\nGeneral Practitioner\n6 Fairway Road\nCorinda\n\naL 4075\n\n09/12/2019\n\nDear Dr. Smith,\nRe: Mrs. Sierra Fredrick, DOB 08/02/1929\n\nYour patient, Mrs. Fredrick, hes experienced a fall at home and was admitted but is now\nready to be discharged after exclusion of any resulting serious injuries or fractures. She\nrequires your ongoing follow up care.\n\nTwo days ago, Mrs, Fredrick was initiaHy brought in by ambulance after falling while\ndescending the stall at home. She was conscious, competent, and oriented to both place\nand person. Her vital signs were normal, but she had a few contusions on the right el§ow.\nHip fracture was suspected. However, she maintained a full range of motion in both her hips\nand was able to ambulate without pain. An x-ray stan of the pelvis and hips excluded any\nfractures but confirmed the presence of osteopenia.\n\nHer ECG and routine tests were normal, and her blood sugar level was at 6.7. HbAIc, thyroid\nfunctions and a mid-stream urine tests were ordered, and the results will be available\ntomorrow. No change has been made regarding her regular medications\n\nMr: Mrs Fredrick requires a geriatric review and to be seen by an endocrinologist for further\nassessment of her osteopenia. In order to decrease her future fall risk, please arrange for a\nassessment by the Aged Care Assessment Team to ensure home and personal assistance.\n\nShould you have any further queries, please do not hesitat